-- title:
--   Kernel ideal of ψ∘χ as an adelic lattice
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of prime characteristic $q'$ that is algebraic over $\mathbb{F}_{q'}$, and let $X_1$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ all of whose $\kappa$-points killed by $q'$ are zero. Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ satisfy $a<0$, $b<0$ and, for every finite place $v$ of $\mathbb{Q}$, the condition that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda_1\subset\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is an order (containing $1$, multiplicatively closed, finitely generated, with $\mathbb{Q}$-span everything) and maximal among orders, and let $\theta_1$ be an injective ring map from the subring generated by the $\kappa$-rational self-homomorphisms of $X_1$ into $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ with image exactly $\Lambda_1$. Fix a unit $x$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\widehat{\mathbb{Q}}$, an elliptic curve $W$, a nonzero $\kappa$-rational homomorphism $\chi\colon X_1\to W$ (i.e. a member of `rationalHomSet`, so zero or represented by rational functions outside a finite set) and a unit $d$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, such that $\theta_1$ carries the kernel ideal $\{\rho\circ\chi:\rho\in\mathrm{Hom}_\kappa(W,X_1)\}$ onto the quaternion conjugate of $d\cdot(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\cap x\widehat{\Lambda}_1)$, where $\widehat{\Lambda}_1$ denotes [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda_1$, the additive group generated by the $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda_1$ and $\alpha$ an integral finite adele, and $\mathbb{H}\cap y\widehat{\Lambda}_1$ is [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19). Let further $W'$ be elliptic, $\psi\colon W\to W'$ a nonzero $\kappa$-rational homomorphism admitting a $\kappa$-rational $\psi'\colon W'\to W$ with $\psi'\circ\psi=n$ and $\psi\circ\psi'=n$ for $n=\#\ker\psi$. Then there exists a unit $g$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\widehat{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose underlying element lies in $\widehat{\Lambda}_1$ such that $\theta_1$ carries the kernel ideal of $\psi\circ\chi$ onto the conjugate of $d\cdot(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\cap xg\widehat{\Lambda}_1)$, and $n^2$ equals the relative index of the additive group $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\cap xg\widehat{\Lambda}_1$ in $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\cap x\widehat{\Lambda}_1$.
--
--   This is the passage from subgroups to lattices in Deuring's correspondence between finite $\kappa$-rational subgroups of $W$ and left ideals of $\operatorname{End}_\kappa X_1$ contained in the kernel ideal $\operatorname{Hom}_\kappa(W,X_1)\chi$, here transported through $\theta_1$ and $J\mapsto\overline{dJ}$ into the adelic description of lattices $\mathbb{H}\cap y\widehat{\Lambda}_1$: composing $\chi$ with a separable isogeny $\psi$ of degree $n$ replaces the idele $x$ by $xg$ with $g$ integral and multiplies the index by $n^2$. It feeds the inductive construction of the supersingular-point dictionary in [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_equiv_ofFiniteIdele_mul_isAddCyclic_forall_ker_eq_of_kernelIdealSet_comp_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_equiv_ofFiniteIdele_mul_isAddCyclic_forall_ker_eq_of_kernelIdealSet_comp_eq).
